decisions:
  - id: D-hook-source-truth
    decision: Hook .sh source files live in src/commands/hooks/scripts/, generated via generate-hooks.mjs
    rationale: Editing plugins/ directly gets overwritten on build. Discovered after 3 failed attempts.
  - id: D-graduation-system
    decision: Built 3-tier automation graduation with data-driven promotion and auto-demotion
    rationale: Agents wasted ~12K tokens/session on compliance checks the stop hook already performs. 5 habits retroactively graduated, saving ~99% of compliance overhead.
  - id: D-never-graduate-list
    decision: tool-called check types cannot graduate — they require agent cognition
    rationale: A hook can verify filesystem state but cannot force an agent to reason about MCP tool output.
  - id: D-drift-phase3-algorithm
    decision: '4-signal weighted scoring for content relocation: first/last line (0.4), structural hash (0.3), Levenshtein (0.2), line count (0.1)'
    rationale: Spec-defined weights balance structural stability (function signatures) with content similarity (variable renames).
learnings:
  - Hook scripts in plugins/ are generated from src/commands/hooks/scripts/*.sh — always edit source, run generate-hooks.mjs
  - 5 of 13 seed habits were already enforced by stop hook checks — marking them graduated eliminates duplicate evaluation
  - Conductor .purpose YAML context items with colons get parsed as objects by strict YAML parsers — quote them
  - SentinelEvent needs Hashable for SwiftUI .popover(item:)
  - Levenshtein on strings >5000 chars should use approximation to avoid O(n*m) blowup
